1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,458
Welcome back.

2
00:00:01,498 --> 00:00:04,837
Take a moment to notice how far you've come these 4 weeks.

3
00:00:04,877 --> 00:00:08,018
Breathe in, and out.

4
00:00:08,058 --> 00:00:10,444
Start with what matters to you most.

5
00:00:10,484 --> 00:00:14,050
On your worksheet, write 3 values you want your future work to honor,

6
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:16,991
and a few strengths that are deeply human.

7
00:00:17,031 --> 00:00:18,401
Maybe empathy,

8
00:00:18,441 --> 00:00:20,647
creativity, judgment, humor.

9
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:23,966
Now think about AI and jobs.

10
00:00:24,006 --> 00:00:25,477
Here's the honest picture.

11
00:00:25,517 --> 00:00:28,585
Some early career roles really are shifting,

12
00:00:28,625 --> 00:00:31,371
especially in the most AI-exposed jobs.

13
00:00:31,411 --> 00:00:33,508
And the overall evidence is mixed.

14
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:36,613
Many employers expect AI to create jobs, too.

15
00:00:36,653 --> 00:00:40,693
So, notice the difference between a fear and a fact.

16
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:45,514
Then, choose one next step that's yours to control in the next two weeks.

17
00:00:45,554 --> 00:00:48,803
Learn a skill, talk to someone in your field,

18
00:00:48,843 --> 00:00:50,995
visit career services.

19
00:00:51,035 --> 00:00:53,492
Write, “My next step is…”

20
00:00:53,532 --> 00:00:54,943
and give it a date.

21
00:00:54,983 --> 00:00:56,419
One step is enough.

22
00:00:56,459 --> 00:01:01,531
You don't have to have the whole future figured out to shape it with intention.
